    "body": "A cheap first layer, suggested by mkinney (who has used it for years): [UptimeRobot](https://uptimerobot.com/) has a free plan, takes a few minutes to set up, and sends email alerts.\n\n- An HTTP or **keyword** monitor on `https://neotech.github.io/Camcraft/app/` (and the site root, for the version string) catches the page going missing, a 404, or the \"not part of this copy\" page replacing the app after a deploy.\n- It does not run the wasm module, so the headless-browser start-up check above stays the way to catch \"the page loads but the shell never starts\". The two together: UptimeRobot for availability within minutes, the daily headless check for \"does it actually start\".\n",
